  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>As we know particle velocity,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mi>&#955;</mi></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Therefore,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mfenced><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>n</mi></math></p><p>Now as we know,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>n</mi></math></p><p>As given in the question,&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mfenced><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>v</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>20</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>n</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></math></p>"
  }
